# VLOnto playbook

*Build, validate, query and use the Vietnamese legal knowledge graph.* Release {{ cfg.release }} (version {{ cfg.version }}), knowledge-graph build of {{ cfg.build_date }}, document validity as of {{ cfg.validity_as_of }}. Author: tmquan.

Related paper: *{{ cite.title | esc }}* ({{ cite.short_authors }}, {{ cite.year }}), [arXiv:{{ cite.arxiv_id }}]({{ cite.url }}).

## 1. Scope, audience and disclaimer

VLOnto is an OWL ontology of Vietnamese law and a knowledge graph built with it from {{ n_src }} public datasets of Vietnamese legal material. In {{ release }} (version {{ cfg.version }}, this release), the graph connects {{ num(st.documents) }} legal documents and their {{ num(st.articles) }} articles (*Điều*) with the {{ num(st.change_events) }} dated events that replaced, amended or repealed them, with {{ num(st.legal_basis_links) }} legal-basis links and {{ num(st.citation_links) }} citation links between documents, and with {{ num(st.legal_questions) }} published legal Q&As, {{ num(st.legal_terms) }} legal terms and {{ num(st.news_articles) }} legal news items. The build writes {{ pub_tables | length }} parquet tables, a full RDF dump of {{ num(st.rdf_triples) }} triples and a browser-sized RDF subset of {{ num(st.core_ttl_triples) }} triples. VLOnto is published as code and a website: the GitHub repository holds the build code, the ontology with SHACL shapes and documentation, a website with 3D playgrounds and a SPARQL playground, and this playbook. The data stays in the {{ n_src }} source datasets, and the knowledge graph is built from them on your own machine (section 2.2).
{% if not cfg.courts_included and deferred %}

**Court decisions join in v2.** {{ release }} is built from the {{ n_src }} thuvienphapluat.vn datasets only. The court datasets {% for d in deferred %}`{{ d }}`{{ " and " if not loop.last else "" }}{% endfor %} (court decisions and precedents, with the provisions they apply) are planned for VLOnto v2 (version {{ planned }}); the judiciary classes and properties stay in the ontology with a scope note that says so (section 4.2). *Bản án, quyết định của Tòa án và án lệ sẽ được bổ sung trong VLOnto v2.*
{% endif %}

**Who this is for.** Engineers who build legal search, question answering or agents over Vietnamese law and need structured validity, citation and Q&A-usage data; legal-technology practitioners who want to query that data without building it; and maintainers who rebuild and release VLOnto. The playbook assumes working knowledge of Python and SQL; SPARQL and OWL are introduced where they are used.

**What it covers.** How to open the offline website and query the files (section 2), how the data flows from the source datasets to the outputs of the build (section 3), the ontology (section 4), how to rebuild the graph (section 5) and how it was validated (section 6), query recipes with their real results (section 7), how to use VLOnto inside the Vietnamese legal assistant agent (section 8), the website (section 9), reproducibility and maintenance (sections 10 and 11) and the known limits (section 12). How to cite VLOnto is in section 1.1, and the references follow section 12. The appendices are generated from the ontology file, the data dictionary and the licence policy.

**Where the numbers come from.** Every number in this playbook is read from the build reports of {{ cfg.build_date }} by `playbook/tools/gather_facts.py`, which also runs every query recipe and code example against that build and stores their output; `playbook/tools/render_md.py` then fills this text. No number is typed by hand, so a rebuild of the graph followed by a rebuild of the playbook updates all of them. All of them describe {{ release_v }}, this release.

> **Not legal advice.** VLOnto is a research and engineering resource. It is not an official legal text and not legal advice. Its relations are extracted automatically from public sources and can be wrong; the validity of {{ num(st.validity.unknown) }} of the {{ num(st.documents) }} documents ({{ pct(st.validity.unknown, st.documents) }}) is unknown. Read the source document (every document, Q&A and term keeps its source URL) and ask a qualified Vietnamese lawyer before relying on any legal conclusion.

