The namespaces are under the website address `https://tmquan.github.io/VLOnto/`. GitHub Pages serves static files without content negotiation, so a client that dereferences an IRI gets a web page or nothing, not RDF: load the Turtle file or the dump instead of dereferencing IRIs.

### 4.6 Versioning

The ontology header carries `owl:versionInfo "{{ o.header.version }}"`, `owl:versionIRI <{{ o.header.version_iri }}>`,{% if o.header.prior_version %} `owl:priorVersion <{{ o.header.prior_version }}>`,{% endif %} `dcterms:created` and `dcterms:modified` ({{ o.header.modified }}) and the licence `<{{ o.header.license }}>`. Release {{ cfg.release }} is version {{ cfg.version }} of the ontology and of the build. Every knowledge-graph build records the same version and its validity date (`vlo:softwareVersion` and `vlo:validityAsOf` on the build activity node). Proposed release policy for the repository, semantic versioning: a patch release changes labels, definitions or data only; a minor release adds classes or properties; a major release renames or removes terms or changes the IRI scheme. Each release keeps its version IRI, so data can state which version it conforms to.

