**Offline use.** Every page is plain HTML with classic scripts: no ES modules, no `fetch`, no server. Data bundles are JavaScript files that assign the JSON to `window.VLONTO` (generated by `tools/json2js.py`), the WebAssembly of Oxigraph is embedded in its script, and the fonts are in the site folder, so the pages work from `file://` without network access. Each bundle stays below 20 MB ({{ f.manifest.files | length }} files listed in `manifest.json` with size and sha256).

**3D views.** The 3D views use three.js and 3d-force-graph with text labels drawn as sprites. The legal-network positions are precomputed in the build (`vlonto.cli layout`), so the page does not run a force simulation on {{ num(net.lengths.nodes) }} nodes. Rendering speed depends on the graphics hardware; the automated website checks render with a software WebGL implementation, so their frame rates say nothing about a real GPU.

